meta {
  name: Revert Invoice Payment
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/payments/{{invoicePaymentId}}/revert
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "reason": "Reverted from Payments ledger"
  }
}

docs {
  Revert a SINGLE invoice receipt — not the whole invoice. The receipt row is kept
  active but its `amount` is zeroed (original preserved in `revertedAmount`), and the
  invoice's paid / outstanding balances and payment + due status are recomputed off
  the REMAINING non-reverted receipts. The invoice stays active, so if it drops out
  of COMPLETED its source orders reappear on the Outstanding report automatically.
  The reverted row stays visible in the Finance → Payments "Reverted" tab.

  Permission `finance:payments__cancel_invoice_payment`. `INVOICE_ALREADY_CANCELLED`
  (409) if the invoice was cancelled; `INVOICE_PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND` (404) if the
  receipt does not resolve / is already reverted. `reason` is optional.
}
